## 2. Information We Process & How It Is Used

CleanMyPhone operates under strict **Data Minimization** principles. The application processes device data locally in temporary RAM to provide storage management utilities.

| Data Type | How It Is Processed | Is Data Uploaded or Shared? |
|---|---|---|
| **Photos & Media** | Analyzed locally using on-device image hashing algorithms to detect duplicate photos and burst shots. | **No.** Never leaves your device. |
| **Videos & Heavy Files** | Read locally to calculate file sizes, durations, and formats for clutter management. | **No.** Never leaves your device. |
| **System Cache & Temp Files** | Scanned in local public/external storage directories to calculate recoverable space. | **No.** Never leaves your device. |
| **Installed Applications** | Package metadata (app name, package ID, APK size, install date, last used timestamp) is read to identify large or inactive apps. | **No.** Never leaves your device. |
| **System RAM & CPU Metrics** | Read in real time from Android Linux system kernels (`/proc/stat`, `ActivityManager`) to display live device performance. | **No.** Never leaves your device. |
| **Network Speed / Bandwidth** | Live data transfer rates are calculated via `TrafficStats` to provide the real-time speedometer tool. | **No.** Never leaves your device. |
| **User Preferences** | Scan settings, dark mode preferences, and notification toggles are stored locally using Android `DataStore` / `SharedPreferences`. | **No.** Stored strictly in local app sandbox. |

