## 3. Permissions & Justification

To perform core storage management and cleaning tasks, CleanMyPhone requests specific Android permissions. Each permission is strictly used for its declared user-facing feature:

### 3.1. All Files Access (`MANAGE_EXTERNAL_STORAGE`)
- **Android Versions:** Android 11 (API 30) and above
- **Purpose:** Required to scan, index, and delete residual junk files, obsolete APK installers, orphan cache files, duplicate downloads, and large files across the internal shared storage.
- **Privacy Assurance:** Only files explicitly selected or confirmed by the user in the Cleanup Basket are modified or deleted.

### 3.2. Read Media Permissions (`READ_MEDIA_IMAGES`, `READ_MEDIA_VIDEO`, `READ_MEDIA_AUDIO`, `READ_EXTERNAL_STORAGE`)
- **Android Versions:** Android 13 (API 33)+ and legacy versions
- **Purpose:** Allows the app to display photo thumbnails, group identical/burst photos for review, and list large video files.
- **Privacy Assurance:** Media files are never uploaded, backed up, or indexed off-device.

### 3.3. Query All Packages (`QUERY_ALL_PACKAGES`) & Usage Stats (`PACKAGE_USAGE_STATS`)
- **Purpose:** Powers the Applications Hub and Inactive Apps Manager by calculating storage consumed by installed applications and identifying apps unused for 30+ days.
- **Privacy Assurance:** No application usage profiling or telemetry is exported.

### 3.4. Accessibility Service (`BIND_ACCESSIBILITY_SERVICE`)
- **Purpose:** An optional, user-initiated utility that automates navigating to system App Info screens to clear app cache files for user-selected applications.
- **Privacy Assurance:** 
  - The accessibility service is **disabled by default** and requires explicit system activation.
  - It is active **only** during an active cache-clearing session.
  - It does **not** read screen text outside system settings, does not record keystrokes, does not intercept passwords or sensitive data, and does not transmit any screen content.

### 3.5. Notifications (`POST_NOTIFICATIONS`)
- **Purpose:** Used solely to deliver local alerts (such as when recoverable storage exceeds user-defined limits or when a deep scan finishes).
- **Privacy Assurance:** Notifications are triggered locally and can be toggled off at any time in Settings.

### 3.6. Advertising ID (`com.google.android.gms.permission.AD_ID`)
- **Purpose:** Used by Google Mobile Ads (AdMob) and OneSignal to serve advertisements and deliver relevant push notifications.
- **Privacy Assurance:** Users can reset or delete their advertising identifier at any time through Android System Settings (*Settings > Google > Ads*).

